From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 08:24:31 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] win32u, wow64win: D3DKMT shared resources: allocations,
 ShareObjects, OpenResource, QueryResourceInfo (3321)

CORE review: graphics. D3DKMTCreateAllocation(2), DestroyAllocation(2),
ShareObjects, OpenResource(2), OpenResourceFromNtHandle, QueryResourceInfo and
QueryResourceInfoFromNtHandle were stubs. A resource is now a block of system
memory in a section: a header, the private runtime and driver data of the
resource and its allocations, and the content of every allocation. A global
share handle names the section in the session's namespace (D3DKMTOpenResource,
QueryResourceInfo), D3DKMTShareObjects hands out NT handles of it (inheritable,
duplicable, optionally named), D3DKMTOpenResourceFromNtHandle and
QueryResourceInfoFromNtHandle open it, in this process or another.

There is no kernel-mode driver, so the conventions a driver would define are in
include/wine/kmtshare.h: the private driver data of an allocation starts with
its content size, and a D3DKMTEscape (DRIVERPRIVATE) maps an allocation, giving
the runtime a section handle and the content's offset and size.

wow64win: the thunks of CreateAllocation(2) and OpenResource(2/FromNtHandle)
read the allocation arrays with the wrong size and stride, never returned the
handles, and CreateAllocation2 called CreateAllocation; rewritten.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XZFS4SPPzeH5d2c1MuzqCS

