+/*
+ * Stained Glass OS: the private interface between a user-mode D3D runtime and
+ * win32u's D3DKMT layer.
+ *
+ * There is no kernel-mode display driver behind win32u's D3DKMT functions.
+ * Allocations live in system memory (sections, so they can be shared between
+ * processes), and the usual driver conventions are defined here:
+ *
+ * - the private driver data of an allocation starts with a struct
+ *   wine_kmt_alloc_data, which says how many bytes of content the allocation
+ *   has; the rest of the data is kept for the opener, as a driver would;
+ * - a D3DKMTEscape of type D3DKMT_ESCAPE_DRIVERPRIVATE whose private data is a
+ *   struct wine_kmt_escape maps an allocation: the runtime gets a section
+ *   handle, and the offset and size of the allocation's content in it.
